Note that we use `static_cast<int>(i)` to convert each element to an `int` before printing it, as `cout` cannot directly print `uint8_t`. Also, we use `std::hex` to set the stream's output format to hexadecimal.

Here's an example C++ function that converts a vector<uint8_t> into a string of numbers:

```c++
#include <iostream>
#include <vector>
#include <sstream>

std::string vectorToString(const std::vector<uint8_t>& v) {
    std::stringstream ss;
    for (auto i = v.begin(); i != v.end(); ++i) {
        ss << static_cast<int>(*i) << ' ';
    }
    return ss.str();
}

int main() {
    std::vector<uint8_t> v = {0x01, 0x23, 0x45, 0x67};
